env
llmdocs
data/
results
**/**.pyc
logs
scratchpad
temp/
# ⛔⛔ CREDENTIALS. .hf_token lives in the repo root (it is where the HF token is
#    kept for the gated google/gemma-2b pull). It was NOT ignored until 2026-08-25
#    and a `git add -A` would have COMMITTED AND PUBLISHED it to a public repo.
.hf_token
*.token
hf_token*
*.log

# ⛔ CLUSTER-MEASURED ARTIFACTS — written ON the cluster, by a probe, and they must
#   NOT travel with the repo. Two reasons, and the second is the expensive one:
#     1. a value measured on narval is meaningless on any other machine, and a
#        committed one is indistinguishable from a measured one (the exact
#        indistinguishability sbatch/narval exists to remove);
#     2. if they were tracked, the FIRST `git pull` after running the probe would
#        refuse with "local changes would be overwritten" -- friction in precisely
#        the workflow this port was built to keep frictionless.
#   ⚠ They are not lost: 00_probe_narval.sh, 03b_probe_gpu_memory.sh and
#     fir_baseline_read.py all PRINT their file into the ./logs transcript.
sbatch/*/measured.sh
sbatch/*/measured_gpu.sh
sbatch/*/baseline_proxy.json
